WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.836
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:01.106 --> 00:02.524
[♪ opening theme song playing]

3
00:43.065 --> 00:48.070
THE PERFECT LIE

4
00:53.158 --> 00:54.743
THIS DRAMA IS A WORK OF FICTION

5
00:54.826 --> 00:58.080
SCENES INVOLVING CHILD ACTORS AND ANIMALS WERE FILMED SAFELY

6
00:58.747 --> 01:00.749
[♪ ominous music playing]

7
01:30.278 --> 01:31.697
[softly] No, that can't be…

8
01:40.330 --> 01:42.624
[clicks tongue] What I do know is,

9
01:42.708 --> 01:45.585
just because we kissed doesn't mean I wanted to have sex with him.

10
01:49.297 --> 01:51.508
Right at that moment, my phone alarm went off.

11
01:53.343 --> 01:58.765
With daylight saving time in effect, the US stock market opens at 10:30 p.m.

12
02:02.477 --> 02:03.562
[Junho taps on phone]

13
02:06.481 --> 02:07.482
Here, you can check.

14
02:17.617 --> 02:18.660
[phone alarm sounds]

15
02:24.124 --> 02:25.125
[alarm intensifies]

16
02:27.127 --> 02:28.128
[sinister sting]

17
02:28.628 --> 02:34.760
EPISODE 2 THAT NIGHT

18
02:34.843 --> 02:36.303
[detective] What happened after the kiss?

19
02:37.763 --> 02:38.764
[Junho exhales sharply]

20
02:38.847 --> 02:41.099
This is ridiculous. How am I supposed to tell you?

21
02:41.183 --> 02:42.893
[team leader] She said it was sexual assault.

22
02:43.602 --> 02:44.603
No.

23
02:56.198 --> 02:57.741
We sat on the couch,

24
02:58.950 --> 03:01.578
had some wine, and talked some more.

25
03:01.661 --> 03:02.746
[typing]

26
03:03.663 --> 03:06.041
Then Ms. Kang took me to the bedroom.

27
03:09.795 --> 03:13.340
Do I really have to go into every single detail?

28
03:13.423 --> 03:15.050
[detective] And after you went into the bedroom?

29
03:17.886 --> 03:18.887
[Junho sighs]

30
03:22.766 --> 03:24.392
We lay down on the bed together.

31
03:24.893 --> 03:26.811
[♪ tense music plays]

32
03:34.027 --> 03:35.779
[detective] Were you on top of her, Mr. Min?

33
03:38.573 --> 03:39.574
Yes.

34
03:40.784 --> 03:42.202
Did you push her down?

35
03:44.120 --> 03:45.539
No, I did not.

36
03:45.622 --> 03:46.706
I told him to stop.

37
03:46.790 --> 03:49.584
I really… I really didn't want it!

38
03:49.668 --> 03:50.919
[sobbing]

39
03:51.002 --> 03:52.921
I really didn't want to do it.

40
03:53.004 --> 03:55.298
[crying, breathing shakily]

41
03:59.511 --> 04:00.679
We kissed and…

42
04:02.222 --> 04:03.473
just naturally…

43
04:05.183 --> 04:07.894
I swear, it wasn't a situation where she'd feel uncomfortable.

44
04:08.895 --> 04:10.355
If anything, it was the opposite.

45
04:11.356 --> 04:15.068
Ms. Kang never pushed me away or resisted.

46
04:16.027 --> 04:19.447
Not once did she tell me to stop.

47
04:21.032 --> 04:23.118
[crying] I don't remember.

48
04:24.077 --> 04:26.538
I don't know when it started.

49
04:35.338 --> 04:36.798
[♪ somber music plays]

50
04:36.882 --> 04:38.300
If I'd known Ms. Kang…

51
04:40.552 --> 04:41.970
didn't want it…

52
04:44.055 --> 04:46.057
I never would've crossed that line.

53
04:49.269 --> 04:51.271
I don't know why she's suddenly doing this.

54
04:58.403 --> 05:00.989
My feelings were genuine. [inhales sharply]

55
05:01.781 --> 05:02.782
[sighs]

56
05:04.075 --> 05:05.827
I wanted to keep seeing her…

57
05:09.748 --> 05:11.291
Maybe even build a future…

58
05:12.751 --> 05:13.752
[sighs]

59
05:18.465 --> 05:19.841
I texted her in the morning

60
05:19.925 --> 05:22.218
and even had some porridge delivered to her.

61
05:23.511 --> 05:25.221
-We confirmed that. -[typing]

62
05:26.348 --> 05:29.726
I mean, if we really didn't have a good time last night,

63
05:29.809 --> 05:31.853
I wouldn't have sent her a text like that, would I?

64
05:33.980 --> 05:35.982
If something like that had actually happened…

65
05:37.734 --> 05:39.027
it makes no sense.

66
05:41.112 --> 05:42.781
[Soyeon] Why Ms. Kang of all people?

67
05:44.491 --> 05:45.659
Because we're close.

68
05:45.742 --> 05:47.619
Did you really not tell her the truth?

69
05:49.079 --> 05:50.246
About what?

70
05:50.330 --> 05:53.750
That I'm the one who sold the sneakers, and that you just let me use your account.

71
06:00.465 --> 06:01.925
You like me, don't you?

72
06:02.467 --> 06:03.885
No, I don't.

73
06:04.552 --> 06:06.304
Then why did you give me this?

74
06:06.388 --> 06:07.472
Is it a knockoff?

75
06:07.555 --> 06:09.224
It's real, okay?

76
06:09.307 --> 06:10.725
Then why did you give it to me?

77
06:12.769 --> 06:14.938
Your shoes and your bag are all knockoffs.

78
06:16.898 --> 06:19.109
I thought you should have at least one real thing…

79
06:19.192 --> 06:20.276
[chuckles]

80
06:21.111 --> 06:23.822
[Soyeon] See? You do like me.

81
06:25.240 --> 06:26.491
I told you, I don't.

82
06:26.992 --> 06:27.993
[Soyeon laughs softly]

83
06:30.578 --> 06:31.579
Sex crime cases--

84
06:31.663 --> 06:32.956
It wasn't a crime.

85
06:38.461 --> 06:39.462
You're sure it wasn't?

86
06:41.464 --> 06:43.091
Yeah, I'm sure.

87
06:46.302 --> 06:47.804
Being too perfect is a crime too.

88
06:50.557 --> 06:52.600
I know you're someone who wouldn't do that,

89
06:53.518 --> 06:55.645
but I'm asking as your attorney.

90
07:00.984 --> 07:01.985
You…

91
07:02.610 --> 07:03.611
don't believe me?

92
07:05.905 --> 07:07.240
Okay, fine.

93
07:07.991 --> 07:09.200
Then I'll represent you.

94
07:10.243 --> 07:11.286
No need.

95
07:11.369 --> 07:14.414
Hey, you don't hire an attorney to cover up lies.

96
07:14.497 --> 07:16.458
You hire one to protect the truth.

97
07:19.627 --> 07:20.628
-[sighs] -First,

98
07:20.712 --> 07:22.672
I'll find out why that woman is doing this.

99
07:23.423 --> 07:25.550
-[door closes] -[kids] Mom!

100
07:25.633 --> 07:26.634
[Jieun] Hey.

101
07:26.718 --> 07:28.553
-[Ugeun] Yay, Auntie's here! -[Uyeong] Yay, Auntie!

102
07:28.636 --> 07:29.971
[Jieun] You didn't put them to bed?

103
07:30.054 --> 07:31.598
-[kids chattering] -They wanted to see you first.

104
07:31.681 --> 07:35.393
Wow, you did such a good job. But it's way past your bedtime.

105
07:35.477 --> 07:37.645
-Auntie's here to sleep too. -[parent] All right, bedtime.

106
07:37.729 --> 07:39.606
-Play with Auntie tomorrow, okay? -[parent] Let's go.

107
07:39.689 --> 07:41.691
But how come you came together?

108
07:42.525 --> 07:44.694
[Jieun] Uh, Jisun wasn't feeling too well.

109
07:45.528 --> 07:47.155
What's wrong? Are you sick?

110
07:48.198 --> 07:49.783
Oh, it's nothing. I just…

111
07:50.492 --> 07:51.659
[Jieun] Go on up.

112
07:57.874 --> 07:59.793
I told her to come and stay with us.

113
07:59.876 --> 08:01.586
I didn't feel right leaving her alone.

114
08:01.669 --> 08:02.962
-Oh… -[Jieun] Yeah.

115
08:05.548 --> 08:07.091
[♪ tense music plays]

116
08:07.175 --> 08:08.176
[sighs]

117
08:27.612 --> 08:28.613
[gasps softly]

118
08:29.781 --> 08:31.115
Sorry.

119
08:31.741 --> 08:33.785
-No, it's okay. -[Jieun] Hmm.

120
08:34.702 --> 08:36.996
I put some blankets and a pillow over there.

121
08:39.541 --> 08:40.542
Thanks.

122
08:41.960 --> 08:43.545
I'm so glad I have you.

123
08:45.672 --> 08:46.673
[Jieun sighs]

124
08:47.549 --> 08:49.008
Give me your door code.

125
08:49.092 --> 08:51.344
I'll go get some things you might need.

126
08:52.971 --> 08:54.973
[♪ tense music plays]

127
08:58.184 --> 08:59.477
[phone buzzing]

128
09:03.398 --> 09:04.399
[sighs]

129
09:07.360 --> 09:09.362
-[taps phone] -[phone buzzing stops]

130
09:34.721 --> 09:35.722
[sighs]

131
10:01.080 --> 10:02.081
[door closes]

132
10:03.666 --> 10:04.667
[footsteps approaching]

133
10:06.294 --> 10:09.297
[detective] You know what DFSA is, right?

134
10:10.131 --> 10:11.758
You're a doctor, so I'm sure you do.

135
10:12.759 --> 10:14.177
What does that mean?

136
10:14.260 --> 10:16.346
Drug-facilitated sexual assault.

137
10:17.555 --> 10:19.182
-The so-called "date-rape drugs." -[scoffs]

138
10:22.185 --> 10:24.145
Why are you telling me this?

139
10:28.107 --> 10:32.612
Ms. Kang Jisun's toxicology screening results are in.

140
10:39.535 --> 10:40.536
[sighs]

141
10:41.663 --> 10:42.664
[gasps]

142
10:44.540 --> 10:45.541
[breathing heavily]

143
11:03.810 --> 11:05.812
[breathing shakily]

144
11:40.763 --> 11:42.223
You're eating breakfast pretty late.

145
11:45.810 --> 11:47.186
[Hyunsoo] You're just getting home now?

146
11:48.313 --> 11:50.315
Yeah, I had a lot of surgeries yesterday.

147
11:51.607 --> 11:53.568
-[liquid pouring] -I figured.

148
11:55.611 --> 11:57.196
Sorry I couldn't call.

149
12:06.414 --> 12:07.749
Dad, are you okay?

150
12:07.832 --> 12:08.833
[Junho] What?

151
12:09.459 --> 12:11.878
[chuckles] I'm just a little tired.

152
12:20.762 --> 12:23.222
Hyunsoo, the truth is…

153
12:27.727 --> 12:30.563
Hey, why haven't you changed yet?

154
12:31.564 --> 12:32.857
It's Saturday.

155
12:37.487 --> 12:38.488
Oh.

156
12:39.697 --> 12:40.698
Right.

157
12:55.755 --> 12:56.756
[whispers] Jisun.

158
13:00.343 --> 13:01.636
Jisun.

159
13:02.970 --> 13:03.971
Hmm.

160
13:05.890 --> 13:07.308
What time is it?

161
13:08.518 --> 13:10.978
[Jieun] A little after 3:00 p.m.

162
13:12.688 --> 13:15.942
How can you keep sleeping like this without eating?

163
13:18.319 --> 13:20.363
I brought some food,

164
13:20.446 --> 13:22.698
so eat something then go back to sleep, okay?

165
13:22.782 --> 13:23.783
[Jisun] Okay.

166
13:29.914 --> 13:31.707
[♪ melancholic music plays]

167
13:36.796 --> 13:38.798
[soft ticking]

168
13:52.270 --> 13:53.271
[sighs]

169
13:59.652 --> 14:01.654
[soft ticking continues]

170
14:18.045 --> 14:20.506
[parent] Aren't you going to tell me what's going on with Jisun?

171
14:22.008 --> 14:23.176
I told you already.

172
14:24.635 --> 14:26.637
-[Uyeong] Dad, I need a straw! -Oh, boy.

173
14:27.430 --> 14:29.891
Goodness, where are the wet wipes?

174
14:32.894 --> 14:36.439
Gosh, you little mess. [chuckles]

175
14:36.522 --> 14:38.566
-Here. -[Jieun] Gosh, you.

176
14:40.067 --> 14:41.694
[parent] Now, don't spill and enjoy.

177
14:42.278 --> 14:43.613
Go on and watch TV.

178
14:50.077 --> 14:52.788
Come on. I know she's not just sick.

179
14:54.248 --> 14:56.250
Is it something you need to hide from me?

180
14:59.629 --> 15:00.922
Don't let anyone know, okay?

181
15:02.465 --> 15:03.466
[parent] Okay.

182
15:03.549 --> 15:05.218
[♪ unsettling music plays]

183
15:05.301 --> 15:08.846
She went on a date with Dr. Min Junho from our hospital,

184
15:08.930 --> 15:10.640
the one she told us about before.

185
15:10.723 --> 15:11.807
Oh, really?

186
15:12.600 --> 15:13.601
And?

187
15:14.393 --> 15:16.604
[no audible dialogue]

188
15:20.441 --> 15:22.652
[♪ unsettling music continues]

189
15:32.370 --> 15:33.996
I seriously can't believe it.

190
15:35.206 --> 15:37.208
Do the police know about what happened before?

191
15:37.291 --> 15:39.502
Why would they need to know?

192
15:39.585 --> 15:41.712
-[parent] Well… -[footsteps approaching]

193
15:43.756 --> 15:46.050
[Jieun] Hey, did you get some sleep?

194
15:46.133 --> 15:47.134
I'm going to work.

195
15:47.218 --> 15:50.179
Have some breakfast before you go.

196
15:50.263 --> 15:51.430
No, I'm good.

197
15:52.181 --> 15:53.683
[Jieun] Hey, Jisun.

198
15:55.017 --> 15:57.395
I think you should take a few more days off.

199
16:01.524 --> 16:02.525
I'm okay.

200
16:03.067 --> 16:04.443
I need to get on with my life.

201
16:11.784 --> 16:13.077
[teacher] Your sister called.

202
16:14.662 --> 16:16.622
Were you so sick you couldn't even call?

203
16:17.456 --> 16:18.624
I'm sorry.

204
16:19.667 --> 16:20.835
[teacher] What was wrong?

205
16:21.544 --> 16:22.962
How sick were you?

206
16:25.965 --> 16:26.966
Well…

207
16:29.302 --> 16:30.720
I'm sorry.

208
16:33.014 --> 16:35.516
[sighs] Next time, no matter how sick you are,

209
16:35.599 --> 16:36.600
call me yourself.

210
16:38.269 --> 16:40.479
You're a teacher. You can't just miss work.

211
16:41.439 --> 16:42.565
Understood?

212
16:43.399 --> 16:44.400
Yes.

213
16:46.485 --> 16:50.114
[teacher] I'll put it down as sick leave and talk to the vice principal.

214
16:50.656 --> 16:53.159
Oh, right. You are teaching during class, right?

215
16:55.745 --> 16:56.746
Yes.

216
16:56.829 --> 17:00.875
These days, parents send their kids with recording devices.

217
17:00.958 --> 17:05.046
Treat every class like the parents are sitting in and observing.

218
17:07.256 --> 17:09.008
You understand what I'm saying, right?

219
17:10.217 --> 17:11.719
Yes, I understand.

220
17:20.227 --> 17:23.439
Soyeon, you must've been busy. But you still managed to finish the book.

221
17:23.522 --> 17:25.816
I read it in the car, while on the move.

222
17:27.610 --> 17:28.694
That's dedication.

223
17:53.594 --> 17:54.804
Here.

224
17:54.887 --> 17:56.055
[Hyunsoo] Ms. Kang.

225
17:56.681 --> 17:58.182
Mine doesn't have a comment.

226
18:03.813 --> 18:05.690
There's a reason there isn't one.

227
18:07.066 --> 18:08.734
-Here you go, Byeongjun. -[Byeongjun] Thank you.

228
18:17.243 --> 18:18.244
[sighs]

229
18:21.747 --> 18:23.416
[♪ unsettling music plays]

230
18:27.128 --> 18:29.755
-[thud] -[students clamoring]

231
18:32.717 --> 18:34.176
[student] Hey! What are you doing?

232
18:34.260 --> 18:36.262
[clamoring continues]

233
18:39.014 --> 18:40.516
What are you guys doing? Stop it!

234
18:40.599 --> 18:43.436
Min Hyunsoo, Yeon Sanghyeon, I said stop!

235
18:43.519 --> 18:44.562
[student 1] Ms. Kang!

236
18:44.645 --> 18:46.188
[Sanghyeon] Let go of me!

237
18:46.772 --> 18:48.274
-[student 2] Let it go! -[Sanghyeon] Let go!

238
18:48.357 --> 18:49.734
-Let go of me! -[student 3] Let it go.

239
18:49.817 --> 18:51.569
What's going on? Why are you fighting?

240
18:51.652 --> 18:52.653
[student 4] Ms. Kang's here.

241
18:56.407 --> 18:58.200
I'm asking you what's going on!

242
18:58.284 --> 18:59.285
[panting]

243
19:00.119 --> 19:02.121
That bastard hit me first.

244
19:02.663 --> 19:05.040
[Jisun] Is that true? Why did you do that?

245
19:08.878 --> 19:10.045
Do you both want demerits?

246
19:10.129 --> 19:11.881
I didn't do anything wrong.

247
19:12.715 --> 19:15.050
-I was just stating facts. -[Hyunsoo] Shut up or I'll kill you!

248
19:15.718 --> 19:16.719
What did you say?

249
19:16.802 --> 19:19.013
-This bastard's dad is a sex offender. -What?

250
19:19.096 --> 19:20.973
My mom saw him getting arrested.

251
19:21.056 --> 19:22.558
[Hyunsoo] You bastard!

252
19:22.641 --> 19:24.977
-No! -[student 5] Guys, stop it!

253
19:25.060 --> 19:27.688
[clamoring resumes, fades]

254
19:27.772 --> 19:29.774
[high-pitched ringing]

255
19:32.818 --> 19:35.654
I've never seen anyone get taken away in handcuffs before.

256
19:35.738 --> 19:37.072
I know.

257
19:38.115 --> 19:40.284
[sighs] What on earth is going on?

258
19:42.328 --> 19:44.663
[Junghyeon] You know, about Dr. Min Junho's wife…

259
19:44.747 --> 19:46.540
How did she die so young?

260
19:46.624 --> 19:47.625
Was it an accident?

261
19:49.835 --> 19:51.962
-[whispering] She took her own life. -Took her own life?

262
19:52.046 --> 19:53.297
[♪ somber music plays]

263
19:53.380 --> 19:54.924
An overdose.

264
19:57.426 --> 19:59.011
[Junghyeon] An overdose…

265
20:08.562 --> 20:09.730
[♪ rousing music plays]

266
20:39.426 --> 20:40.427
[rain pattering]

267
20:48.060 --> 20:49.061
[door lock chimes]

268
20:55.109 --> 20:56.110
[both chuckle]

269
21:04.118 --> 21:05.119
[door lock chimes]

270
21:21.427 --> 21:23.429
[♪ stirring music plays]

271
21:44.575 --> 21:45.576
[shudders]

272
21:58.964 --> 22:02.009
-[doorbell rings] -[gasps]

273
22:09.099 --> 22:10.142
Have a seat.

274
22:12.227 --> 22:14.605
[detective] You have a nice place. You even have a yard.

275
22:14.688 --> 22:16.148
[chuckles] Thank you.

276
22:16.857 --> 22:18.150
I saw that you own the place.

277
22:19.652 --> 22:20.986
It's mostly mortgaged.

278
22:24.573 --> 22:27.743
[team leader] Still, the payments must be pretty steep to handle on your own.

279
22:31.413 --> 22:32.414
Well…

280
22:32.498 --> 22:33.874
It's the same for everyone.

281
22:34.667 --> 22:36.585
But are you here to check out the house?

282
22:37.419 --> 22:40.172
Oh, no. Of course not. [inhales sharply]

283
22:40.798 --> 22:44.593
Uh, Mr. Min has been released for now, and the investigation is ongoing.

284
22:46.345 --> 22:50.683
[detective] Our job is to uncover the truth through our investigation.

285
22:51.850 --> 22:54.853
First of all, neither you nor Mr. Min had any physical injuries.

286
22:54.937 --> 22:57.773
How badly do I have to be hurt for it to count as sexual assault?

287
23:03.529 --> 23:07.783
The blood test also showed nothing unusual other than alcohol.

288
23:07.866 --> 23:11.954
And witnesses at the restaurant said you seemed to be getting along well.

289
23:12.037 --> 23:15.207
There's also security footage of you laughing together on your way home.

290
23:15.290 --> 23:16.917
Because that was before it happened!

291
23:17.459 --> 23:19.712
Right, but… [inhales sharply]

292
23:19.795 --> 23:21.505
…aside from your conflicting statements,

293
23:21.588 --> 23:24.883
we don't have much evidence to go on, and that's making things difficult for us.

294
23:24.967 --> 23:28.053
I should take note of that. Next time, I'll have evidence ready.

295
23:33.976 --> 23:37.271
Have you had men come over for drinks before too?

296
23:37.354 --> 23:38.772
No. Never.

297
23:39.898 --> 23:41.608
So having Mr. Min come into your home

298
23:41.692 --> 23:43.736
-was unusual for you. -Yes.

299
23:43.819 --> 23:46.280
If it weren't for the rain, I never would've let him in!

300
23:46.363 --> 23:50.284
Mr. Min says you were the one who led him from the living room into the bedroom.

301
23:50.367 --> 23:51.869
That's a lie!

302
23:52.703 --> 23:54.705
So it was in bed that you--

303
23:54.788 --> 23:55.789
Yes.

304
23:56.790 --> 24:00.002
You stated that you clearly told him you didn't want to.

305
24:00.085 --> 24:02.296
-Was that at that point as well? -Yes! That's why… [sighs]

306
24:04.006 --> 24:06.216
[♪ tense music plays]

307
24:07.634 --> 24:08.635
[Jisun sighs]

308
24:10.846 --> 24:11.889
I couldn't move.

309
24:11.972 --> 24:13.390
I'm not lying!

310
24:14.975 --> 24:17.102
We have to ask as part of the procedure.

311
24:19.772 --> 24:21.607
I tried to push him away, but I was…

312
24:25.986 --> 24:28.363
I was so shocked that I couldn't move…

313
24:30.949 --> 24:33.202
and I don't remember anything from a certain point.

314
24:35.370 --> 24:39.041
You were the one who asked him out to dinner, correct?

315
24:39.124 --> 24:41.043
I didn't ask him out. I accepted his invitation!

316
24:41.126 --> 24:44.254
You were the one who invited him in

317
24:45.089 --> 24:47.424
and also offered him wine.

318
24:48.175 --> 24:49.968
[scoffs] So?

319
24:51.428 --> 24:53.138
Does that make it okay?

320
25:01.814 --> 25:02.815
[car door closes]

321
25:11.365 --> 25:12.533
[liquid pouring]

322
25:12.616 --> 25:14.618
[♪ unsettling music plays]

323
25:20.958 --> 25:21.959
[sighs]

324
26:10.382 --> 26:11.383
[phone ringing]

325
26:14.386 --> 26:15.929
-Hey, Jisun. -Did you clear away

326
26:16.013 --> 26:17.764
the wine glasses that were on the coffee table?

327
26:18.974 --> 26:22.019
[stammers] No, there was nothing there.

328
26:22.603 --> 26:23.604
[exhales shakily]

329
26:27.941 --> 26:29.818
-[sniffles] -Why?

330
26:30.611 --> 26:32.446
-What is it, Jisun? -[sobbing]

331
26:33.155 --> 26:34.573
It was the wine.

332
26:35.657 --> 26:37.618
-The wine? -[breathing shakily]

333
26:38.869 --> 26:40.704
Did he force you to drink?

334
26:40.787 --> 26:43.916
Min Junho must've spiked my wine!

335
26:43.999 --> 26:45.000
[breathing heavily]

336
26:48.670 --> 26:50.672
SEEKING REPORTS FROM VICTIMS

337
26:50.756 --> 26:53.508
OF DRUG-FACILITATED SEXUAL ASSAULT SYMPTOMS

338
26:53.592 --> 26:56.887
AFTER TAKING GHB, ALSO KNOWN AS A "DATE-RAPE DRUG"

339
26:56.970 --> 26:58.847
CAN TAKE AWAY EVERYTHING FROM YOUR MEMORIES

340
26:58.931 --> 27:01.308
COMMON SYMPTOMS INCLUDE DIZZINESS, NAUSEA, OR VOMITING

341
27:01.391 --> 27:03.810
DESPITE NOT HAVING CONSUMED EXCESSIVE AMOUNTS OF ALCOHOL…

342
27:03.894 --> 27:05.229
[phone clatters]

343
27:08.273 --> 27:10.400
[Jisun] I know I left the wine glasses on the coffee table.

344
27:10.484 --> 27:12.444
But he washed them and put them on the rack!

345
27:13.904 --> 27:16.823
[exhales heavily] No way. You think he drugged you?

346
27:17.449 --> 27:19.159
Why else would he wash the glasses?

347
27:22.579 --> 27:24.122
That's why I couldn't fight back.

348
27:24.706 --> 27:26.083
That's why I couldn't get away.

349
27:26.166 --> 27:28.502
And that's why I can't remember anything!

350
27:28.585 --> 27:30.128
But the test results didn't show--

351
27:30.212 --> 27:31.713
-I looked it up, and GHB-- -I know.

352
27:32.506 --> 27:34.091
It leaves your system within a few hours,

353
27:34.174 --> 27:36.259
and after 12 hours, there's no trace of it.

354
27:36.760 --> 27:39.221
He planned the whole thing from the start.

355
27:40.222 --> 27:43.392
A woman who lives alone brought him home and even gave him wine,

356
27:43.475 --> 27:46.645
so now he can say I'm falsely accusing an innocent man, a successful doctor!

357
27:46.728 --> 27:48.563
Jisun, Jisun.

358
27:48.647 --> 27:50.524
Let's not jump to conclusions.

359
27:51.024 --> 27:52.526
Like you said,

360
27:52.609 --> 27:55.404
he didn't even know he'd end up at your place drinking with you.

361
27:55.487 --> 27:57.531
So the idea that Dr. Min came prepared with drugs…

362
27:58.740 --> 28:00.283
Something doesn't add up.

363
28:08.625 --> 28:10.460
[Junho] You must be really close with your sister.

364
28:11.336 --> 28:13.630
She mentioned you from time to time.

365
28:13.714 --> 28:14.715
[♪ slow music plays]

366
28:14.798 --> 28:16.717
So I knew her sister was a teacher.

367
28:18.677 --> 28:19.803
That's not fair.

368
28:21.179 --> 28:22.806
I hardly know anything about you.

369
28:23.890 --> 28:27.310
Other than what everyone else knows, that you're a respected,

370
28:27.394 --> 28:29.354
well-known doctor, and a great father.

371
28:29.438 --> 28:30.439
[chuckles]

372
28:33.900 --> 28:34.901
[Jisun laughs]

373
28:41.408 --> 28:43.326
-[crickets chirping] -[waves crashing]

374
29:09.019 --> 29:10.562
Can we talk for a minute?

375
29:10.645 --> 29:12.397
Stay away from me. I'll call the police.

376
29:17.944 --> 29:20.697
-[Junho] Just let me ask you one thing. -Stay away! I said stay away!

377
29:24.367 --> 29:25.494
Why did you do it?

378
29:34.211 --> 29:35.670
I could ask you the same thing.

379
29:39.674 --> 29:40.717
Are you really saying…

380
29:41.676 --> 29:42.677
I forced you?

381
29:43.637 --> 29:44.763
You're saying you didn't?

382
29:44.846 --> 29:47.140
I really didn't force you.

383
29:47.224 --> 29:49.184
You think I wouldn't know? It happened to me.

384
29:49.267 --> 29:50.519
It happened to me too.

385
29:53.647 --> 29:54.731
Jisun…

386
29:58.193 --> 30:01.947
If I moved too fast, I'm really sorry.

387
30:02.030 --> 30:03.115
But…

388
30:04.074 --> 30:06.743
-If you'd told me to stop-- -I did tell you to stop!

389
30:11.206 --> 30:12.582
No, you didn't.

390
30:14.459 --> 30:17.921
Maybe you thought it, but you never said it.

391
30:18.004 --> 30:19.756
-I did! -I'm telling you, you didn't!

392
30:19.840 --> 30:22.551
I'm telling you, I did! [breathing shakily]

393
30:27.430 --> 30:28.598
-[Junho sighs] -[sobs]

394
30:29.891 --> 30:30.892
[whimpers]

395
30:33.687 --> 30:35.188
I guess we see things…

396
30:37.149 --> 30:38.358
very differently.

397
30:38.441 --> 30:39.526
You need to leave.

398
30:40.735 --> 30:41.820
-That day… -[Jisun gasps]

399
30:49.786 --> 30:51.037
Why did you meet with me?

400
30:52.581 --> 30:54.583
[♪ unsettling music plays]

401
31:07.929 --> 31:10.932
[Junho] I liked you from the start.

402
31:11.808 --> 31:13.643
From the day we met for the consultation…

403
31:13.727 --> 31:15.103
No, honestly…

404
31:17.105 --> 31:20.275
from the very first day we met by chance…

405
31:22.944 --> 31:25.947
I wanted to see you again for something more serious.

406
31:31.411 --> 31:34.623
I thought we really clicked.

407
31:37.083 --> 31:38.919
Didn't you feel the same way?

408
31:40.545 --> 31:41.546
[chuckles]

409
31:44.174 --> 31:46.259
I don't know if you remember, but…

410
31:48.220 --> 31:49.387
that night…

411
31:52.599 --> 31:54.768
felt so natural.

412
31:58.647 --> 32:03.777
Honestly, it was the best night I'd had in years.

413
32:08.448 --> 32:10.659
-I thought you felt the same way-- -I trusted you.

414
32:12.160 --> 32:15.413
[crying] I trusted you!

415
32:17.499 --> 32:19.668
I wanted to be in love!

416
32:19.751 --> 32:21.753
Not be a victim of a crime!

417
32:29.344 --> 32:30.553
You're misunderstanding me.

418
32:32.514 --> 32:34.182
-I really… -Don't come any closer.

419
32:34.266 --> 32:35.684
Don't come any closer!

420
32:41.022 --> 32:42.315
Jisun…

421
32:48.196 --> 32:49.197
[sighs]

422
32:51.366 --> 32:53.410
You're not referring the case for prosecution?

423
32:54.035 --> 32:55.996
The victim won't just sit back and take it.

424
32:57.622 --> 33:01.084
In a sexual assault case with no evidence, what's the first criterion

425
33:01.167 --> 33:03.545
for determining whether the victim's statement is credible?

426
33:04.671 --> 33:06.756
-Consistency. -Second?

427
33:08.383 --> 33:10.885
[stammers] I'll go move the car first.

428
33:10.969 --> 33:12.887
That little… Second?

429
33:12.971 --> 33:13.972
[groans]

430
33:14.055 --> 33:16.057
-Second. -Oh, right.

431
33:16.558 --> 33:19.561
"Does this make sense logically?" So, reasonableness.

432
33:19.644 --> 33:20.937
Third.

433
33:21.021 --> 33:22.522
[stammers] Third…

434
33:23.106 --> 33:26.443
We still haven't found any motive for her to give a false statement.

435
33:27.235 --> 33:30.363
Let's say her statement, as the alleged victim, was consistent.

436
33:30.447 --> 33:32.157
But it isn't reasonable.

437
33:32.657 --> 33:34.743
-Let's assume she's lying. -[♪ unsettling music plays]

438
33:34.826 --> 33:36.077
Then what do you think?

439
33:36.161 --> 33:39.539
He's a doctor with money and a good reputation.

440
33:39.622 --> 33:42.542
-A perfect target for a big settlement. -What about a polygraph?

441
33:43.585 --> 33:44.919
So what if we do one?

442
33:45.003 --> 33:46.629
It's not admissible as evidence.

443
33:49.132 --> 33:50.300
[footsteps approaching]

444
33:57.140 --> 33:59.100
[♪ tense music plays]

445
33:59.184 --> 34:00.560
How can he be found innocent?

446
34:01.061 --> 34:04.898
Innocence is for the court to decide. That's not our determination to make.

447
34:06.232 --> 34:08.860
We're closing the case without referring it for prosecution.

448
34:08.943 --> 34:12.405
There's insufficient evidence, so it's being closed with no charges.

449
34:12.489 --> 34:14.866
No charges? How does that make any sense?

450
34:14.949 --> 34:17.744
Min Junho washed the wine glasses. Why would he have done that?

451
34:19.913 --> 34:21.247
Why do you think he did it?

452
34:21.331 --> 34:22.457
To destroy the evidence.

453
34:23.249 --> 34:27.045
-He must've drugged me. I'm sure of it. -As you know…

454
34:28.755 --> 34:30.673
your blood test didn't show anything.

455
34:30.757 --> 34:32.675
GHB. The date-rape drug!

456
34:35.845 --> 34:39.099
I'm the victim. How could you let him go without even saying a word to me?

457
34:39.182 --> 34:42.102
The police aren't required to get the victim's consent

458
34:42.185 --> 34:43.770
before making that decision.

459
34:44.396 --> 34:47.690
If you'd like, you can file a request for disclosure.

460
34:55.573 --> 34:56.574
You people…

461
34:57.534 --> 34:59.661
Would you do this if it happened to your family?

462
35:00.912 --> 35:03.748
How can you not be angry about something like this?

463
35:05.375 --> 35:06.960
I understand how you feel, but…

464
35:08.962 --> 35:11.965
this is the outcome based on investigative principles and procedures.

465
35:16.428 --> 35:19.097
Nothing is ever completely someone else's problem.

466
35:22.642 --> 35:24.602
You'll understand once it happens to you.

467
35:26.980 --> 35:28.481
Please apologize before you leave.

468
35:28.565 --> 35:30.692
You should apologize to me first!

469
35:42.412 --> 35:44.497
[door opens, closes]

470
35:45.039 --> 35:47.333
[team leader] She just threatened a police officer, right?

471
35:55.842 --> 35:57.010
[inhales sharply]

472
35:57.093 --> 35:58.094
[phone buzzing]

473
36:03.183 --> 36:06.144
INCOMING CALL JUNGHYEON

474
36:12.275 --> 36:15.904
[Jisun] Do you know how women can avoid being sexually assaulted in the summer?

475
36:21.367 --> 36:23.536
I don't know. Watch what they wear?

476
36:25.538 --> 36:26.831
There's no way.

477
36:30.668 --> 36:33.463
Just like it's not a child's fault when they're sexually abused,

478
36:34.923 --> 36:37.509
anyone can be sexually assaulted if they're unlucky enough.

479
36:39.844 --> 36:42.013
-Well, of course. -But see?

480
36:45.809 --> 36:47.268
You just said it was the clothes,

481
36:47.352 --> 36:49.395
like the victim somehow brought it themselves.

482
36:54.734 --> 36:57.320
Don't treat everyone you know like they're a criminal.

483
36:58.321 --> 36:59.697
I want to kill that bastard too.

484
37:00.448 --> 37:01.616
[footsteps approaching]

485
37:09.415 --> 37:11.334
You said you had something to tell me.

486
37:12.377 --> 37:13.670
It's about Min Junho.

487
37:17.632 --> 37:18.842
What?

488
37:21.928 --> 37:24.138
[whispering] Do you know how that bastard's wife died?

489
37:24.222 --> 37:26.224
[♪ haunting music plays]

490
37:31.604 --> 37:33.481
She took her own life, an overdose.

491
37:37.193 --> 37:38.903
-No way. -[Junghyeon] Yeah.

492
37:40.864 --> 37:44.033
Apparently, she had depression. I mean, he's a doctor.

493
37:44.117 --> 37:46.327
Unless he let it happen, or it was intentional…

494
37:47.245 --> 37:49.747
Drugs to commit a crime and a wife dead from an overdose.

495
37:49.831 --> 37:51.624
Isn't that too much of a coincidence?

496
37:54.419 --> 37:56.629
He's a doctor, but psychiatry isn't his specialty.

497
37:56.713 --> 37:58.298
And he'd still need a prescription.

498
37:58.381 --> 38:01.968
Whenever a medical facility closes, it's always the drugs that go missing.

499
38:02.719 --> 38:05.597
If a medical professional is determined, there's no stopping them.

500
38:08.850 --> 38:12.520
Who knows what kind of drugs that bastard might have hidden in his house?

501
38:16.566 --> 38:19.777
I don't want to drag a dead person into this just to tie it to my case.

502
38:20.778 --> 38:22.322
I'll pretend I never heard that.

503
38:45.470 --> 38:46.471
Here.

504
38:49.182 --> 38:51.059
Enough with the attitude.

505
38:54.020 --> 38:55.063
I said, that's enough.

506
38:55.146 --> 38:56.230
Why were you arrested?

507
39:01.486 --> 39:04.447
I heard you got arrested at the hospital. Why did they arrest you?

508
39:06.824 --> 39:09.410
-Who told you that? -I'm asking you why they arrested you!

509
39:15.625 --> 39:16.834
Hyunsoo.

510
39:18.544 --> 39:22.090
"Dad, someone told me something like that happened."

511
39:22.590 --> 39:25.093
"Is that true?" That's how you should ask.

512
39:27.971 --> 39:29.305
Are you a sex offender?

513
39:44.737 --> 39:48.574
I met this woman.

514
39:55.373 --> 39:57.375
And I thought she was a good person.

515
39:58.793 --> 40:00.253
I thought maybe she could even be

516
40:01.254 --> 40:03.131
a good mom to you.

517
40:06.300 --> 40:07.844
I don't need a mom.

518
40:08.428 --> 40:09.429
[smacks lips]

519
40:11.806 --> 40:14.475
The first time I asked her out on a date, she turned me down.

520
40:15.268 --> 40:17.061
The second time, she said yes.

521
40:18.855 --> 40:21.190
-So we had dinner together… -[♪ gentle music plays]

522
40:21.274 --> 40:26.612
…went to her place, had some wine, and talked…

523
40:27.864 --> 40:29.949
We had a good time.

524
40:32.702 --> 40:34.287
She was the first…

525
40:37.331 --> 40:38.583
since your mom.

526
40:45.256 --> 40:46.883
Then I came home.

527
40:51.054 --> 40:52.221
That's it?

528
40:54.640 --> 40:55.641
[Junho] Yeah.

529
40:57.643 --> 40:59.604
But the next day, the police came to see me.

530
41:01.731 --> 41:03.274
They said I'd done something wrong.

531
41:12.033 --> 41:13.493
I was questioned by the police,

532
41:15.203 --> 41:17.330
and they let me go because they found nothing.

533
41:17.914 --> 41:19.832
Then why would she do that?

534
41:21.751 --> 41:22.919
I don't know.

535
41:24.462 --> 41:25.588
Maybe…

536
41:27.131 --> 41:29.759
there was something she wanted from me.

537
41:31.761 --> 41:32.762
Money?

538
41:33.429 --> 41:34.639
Probably.

539
41:36.808 --> 41:37.809
[sighs]

540
41:38.351 --> 41:39.811
She's a bad person.

541
41:43.606 --> 41:45.983
[Junho] Remember when you went to the police station

542
41:47.026 --> 41:51.364
after you got caught trying to sell those fake sneakers?

543
41:54.492 --> 41:57.703
I knew you didn't do it.

544
42:00.540 --> 42:01.874
How did you know?

545
42:03.501 --> 42:04.627
Because I trust you.

546
42:06.963 --> 42:08.631
I know my son isn't that kind of kid.

547
42:10.883 --> 42:13.511
You probably trusted me too.

548
42:13.594 --> 42:17.140
That's why you felt betrayed and started acting out like that.

549
42:17.974 --> 42:18.975
[sighs]

550
42:19.517 --> 42:20.518
Still,

551
42:21.936 --> 42:23.813
everyone at school knows.

552
42:33.322 --> 42:34.323
Min Hyunsoo.

553
42:35.366 --> 42:36.868
Hold your head high.

554
42:38.286 --> 42:40.329
I'm a victim, and so are you.

555
42:42.623 --> 42:46.711
Victims have to hold their heads high for there to be any justice in this world.

556
42:50.173 --> 42:52.175
[♪ soft music plays]

557
43:13.404 --> 43:14.614
Good morning.

558
43:36.886 --> 43:38.221
[phone buzzes]

559
43:47.355 --> 43:48.356
[door lock chimes]

560
43:54.695 --> 43:56.948
Looks like you didn't sleep well.

561
43:57.782 --> 43:58.824
Why?

562
44:00.326 --> 44:03.454
You think insomnia might make me mistake a date for a crime?

563
44:08.501 --> 44:10.670
I've handled a lot of cases like this.

564
44:13.172 --> 44:15.925
So I can usually tell right away if someone is really a victim.

565
44:18.636 --> 44:21.097
It's a kind of instinct I've developed.

566
44:26.560 --> 44:28.229
But with this case…

567
44:30.648 --> 44:32.108
Honestly, it's hard to tell.

568
44:35.361 --> 44:36.612
[Junho] A toxicology screening?

569
44:38.281 --> 44:39.282
Did Jisun ask for it?

570
44:40.157 --> 44:41.158
It's a routine test.

571
44:41.242 --> 44:45.204
There's nothing routine about treating your date like a drug offender.

572
44:47.623 --> 44:50.042
You're not asking what the results were.

573
44:53.087 --> 44:56.966
Mr. Min didn't care about the test results at all.

574
44:59.969 --> 45:02.888
One of you is clearly lying.

575
45:04.348 --> 45:05.975
But it's not just a lie.

576
45:07.852 --> 45:10.062
It's intricately woven into the truth.

577
45:18.821 --> 45:20.990
Isn't there any way to find out who's lying?

578
45:27.246 --> 45:30.249
Would you be willing to take a polygraph?

579
45:30.958 --> 45:32.960
[door slides open]

580
45:36.881 --> 45:38.466
[Jisun] He'll do it too, right?

581
45:40.343 --> 45:41.385
[Junho] What's going on?

582
45:43.137 --> 45:44.263
[nurse] Oh.

583
45:44.347 --> 45:47.350
We were told Dr. An would be performing the surgery.

584
45:51.312 --> 45:52.313
[Junho sighs]

585
46:12.291 --> 46:13.334
Dr. Kang.

586
46:18.255 --> 46:20.800
-Can you tell your sister-- -Don't talk about my sister.

587
46:20.883 --> 46:22.510
No, please make sure you tell her this.

588
46:24.804 --> 46:26.013
[Jieun sighs]

589
46:26.097 --> 46:27.598
I don't know why she's doing this,

590
46:28.557 --> 46:29.558
but that night…

591
46:31.602 --> 46:32.728
I was really happy.

592
46:35.022 --> 46:37.608
I've probably told more lies than I can count in my life.

593
46:39.360 --> 46:40.861
But I meant what I just said.

594
46:45.866 --> 46:46.992
[Junho exhales deeply]

595
46:50.329 --> 46:53.165
Don't perform surgery, don't do rounds.

596
46:53.249 --> 46:55.334
Are you telling me to leave the hospital?

597
46:58.170 --> 47:01.173
-Director. The investigation is over. -[door opens]

598
47:01.257 --> 47:03.592
I was cleared. There are no charges against me.

599
47:06.011 --> 47:07.888
I was falsely accused. I'm the victim here.

600
47:07.972 --> 47:10.057
How does that damage the hospital's reputation?

601
47:12.476 --> 47:13.477
[exhales sharply]

602
47:15.855 --> 47:16.856
Okay, I understand.

603
47:18.566 --> 47:19.733
[call ends]

604
47:19.817 --> 47:22.778
Your Mr. Perfect image is completely ruined.

605
47:23.779 --> 47:26.031
Oh, wait. It's not just an image.

606
47:26.115 --> 47:27.533
You really are Mr. Perfect.

607
47:29.285 --> 47:31.203
You got played by a gold digger, didn't you?

608
47:32.246 --> 47:33.372
That's not what happened.

609
47:33.456 --> 47:36.667
[scoffs] Don't be so naive.

610
47:37.626 --> 47:41.213
People like us get respected around here.

611
47:41.297 --> 47:44.216
But out there, we're just suckers waiting to be taken advantage of.

612
47:46.427 --> 47:47.845
I trust people.

613
47:48.596 --> 47:49.889
And this isn't a big deal.

614
47:51.307 --> 47:52.308
All right.

615
47:52.391 --> 47:54.560
That's probably why you were released so quickly.

616
47:54.643 --> 47:55.853
Don't worry too much.

617
47:55.936 --> 47:58.397
The hospital's busy, and people forget things fast.

618
47:59.023 --> 48:02.568
But since the director gave the order, stay out of the OR for a while.

619
48:03.402 --> 48:05.529
And you might want to look into other hospitals.

620
48:06.113 --> 48:07.198
Good luck.

621
48:12.411 --> 48:13.412
[sighs]

622
48:14.872 --> 48:16.624
[phone buzzing]

623
48:23.339 --> 48:24.340
Hello?

624
48:27.801 --> 48:30.679
Is there anything left for us to discuss?

625
48:33.224 --> 48:36.560
Why did you wash the wine glasses?

626
48:37.228 --> 48:38.229
[scoffs]

627
48:39.438 --> 48:42.691
Why leave out the fact that I washed the cheese plate too?

628
48:47.112 --> 48:50.074
As you know, I take care of my own household.

629
48:50.824 --> 48:54.411
So I'm in the habit of washing dishes as soon as I see them.

630
48:55.871 --> 48:57.623
The next day was a weekday,

631
48:57.706 --> 49:01.502
and I thought Ms. Kang might be busy in the morning, so I washed them.

632
49:02.461 --> 49:03.837
What, is that illegal too?

633
49:06.215 --> 49:07.216
No.

634
49:13.430 --> 49:17.977
Medical care is built on trust between a doctor and a patient.

635
49:18.602 --> 49:21.814
But now my whole life is falling apart.

636
49:22.481 --> 49:25.859
How far is this going to go? How long is this going to keep happening?

637
49:28.112 --> 49:32.491
I'm asking for your understanding until the investigation is officially closed.

638
49:35.202 --> 49:36.203
[sighs]

639
49:39.331 --> 49:41.542
You could file a false accusation complaint

640
49:41.625 --> 49:45.129
and prove your innocence.

641
49:45.212 --> 49:47.047
She's my son's teacher.

642
49:48.465 --> 49:49.758
For his sake,

643
49:51.010 --> 49:53.345
I don't want to make this any bigger than it already is.

644
49:55.806 --> 49:58.851
Ms. Kang doesn't seem to feel the same way.

645
50:02.605 --> 50:04.982
-She's agreed to take a polygraph. -[♪ soft, tense music plays]

646
50:05.649 --> 50:09.486
Your statements conflict, so if the results support her account,

647
50:10.070 --> 50:12.448
we'll probably reopen the investigation based on that.

648
50:13.532 --> 50:17.411
Polygraph results aren't even admissible as evidence in court.

649
50:17.911 --> 50:21.957
They can be used as indirect evidence depending on the circumstances.

650
50:23.709 --> 50:29.089
The truth should be judged by a person's conscience, not by a machine.

651
50:30.591 --> 50:32.760
I don't believe we should hand over

652
50:33.260 --> 50:35.471
even the last shred of human dignity to a machine.

653
50:35.554 --> 50:38.307
It's more science than machine.

654
50:38.390 --> 50:39.683
And it's fairly accurate.

655
50:42.603 --> 50:43.896
[Junho] I'm a doctor.

656
50:43.979 --> 50:47.691
When someone lies, a certain psychological change occurs,

657
50:48.192 --> 50:52.154
and that change has to produce a corresponding physiological response.

658
50:53.405 --> 50:56.992
But those changes and responses can never be consistent.

659
50:59.161 --> 51:00.746
In the end, it's just statistics.

660
51:03.749 --> 51:05.334
Statistics is science too.

661
51:07.294 --> 51:10.464
If you have nothing to hide, why not take the test?

662
51:11.382 --> 51:12.841
If you haven't lied,

663
51:12.925 --> 51:15.260
it could help show that you didn't commit any crimes.

664
51:15.969 --> 51:17.513
I haven't lied about anything.

665
51:18.389 --> 51:19.431
Exactly.

666
51:22.976 --> 51:26.397
-[button clicks] -[examiner] Is your name Kang Jisun?

667
51:27.523 --> 51:28.857
[button clicks]

668
51:28.941 --> 51:29.942
Yes.

669
51:33.445 --> 51:35.823
[examiner] Are you a contract teacher-librarian?

670
51:37.241 --> 51:38.242
Yes.

671
51:38.867 --> 51:40.994
[examiner] Have you ever been married?

672
51:42.663 --> 51:43.789
No.

673
51:46.166 --> 51:47.167
[mic feedback]

674
51:48.627 --> 51:51.547
[examiner] Were you attracted to Mr. Min Junho?

675
51:53.215 --> 51:54.967
[♪ tense music plays]

676
51:55.050 --> 51:59.680
WERE YOU ATTRACTED TO MR. MIN JUNHO?

677
52:04.309 --> 52:05.561
[polygraph beeping]

678
52:13.402 --> 52:14.695
Yes, at first.

679
52:17.740 --> 52:18.741
[Junho] But…

680
52:19.658 --> 52:20.659
I am curious.

681
52:25.497 --> 52:27.249
People don't believe me.

682
52:28.041 --> 52:29.585
But I wonder if a machine will.

683
52:31.170 --> 52:32.921
-Then… -Let's do it.

684
52:33.922 --> 52:35.257
The polygraph.

685
52:40.929 --> 52:43.599
[examiner] Is your name Min Junho?

686
52:43.682 --> 52:44.683
[button clicks]

687
52:45.434 --> 52:46.435
Yes.

688
52:48.270 --> 52:50.606
-[button clicks] -[examiner] Are you a doctor?

689
52:53.776 --> 52:55.444
Yes, I'm a cardiovascular surgeon.

690
52:58.906 --> 53:00.699
Are you homosexual?

691
53:03.118 --> 53:04.161
No.

692
53:06.079 --> 53:09.500
[examiner] Do you have any memories of being sexually harassed as a child?

693
53:11.835 --> 53:13.128
Yes. In middle school.

694
53:15.088 --> 53:16.298
[examiner] Was that the first time?

695
53:22.179 --> 53:23.180
Yes.

696
53:25.432 --> 53:29.895
My sister was away on a school trip, so I went home alone that day.

697
53:36.068 --> 53:38.445
[examiner] Did you know any of them?

698
53:40.489 --> 53:42.950
[Jisun] I don't know. It was a long time ago.

699
53:44.618 --> 53:46.078
They were from the neighborhood,

700
53:46.161 --> 53:47.746
so I probably saw them around.

701
53:53.961 --> 53:58.549
[examiner] Do you want revenge on the boys who sexually harassed you back then?

702
54:00.759 --> 54:01.885
Revenge?

703
54:08.141 --> 54:10.227
[examiner] Do you want them to be punished?

704
54:14.606 --> 54:17.651
I want them to know exactly what they did.

705
54:21.822 --> 54:23.907
[examiner] Are you angry at Mr. Min Junho?

706
54:23.991 --> 54:26.493
ARE YOU ANGRY AT MR. MIN JUNHO AT THE MOMENT?

707
54:31.164 --> 54:32.165
Yes.

708
54:36.420 --> 54:39.131
Do you want to kill Min Junho?

709
54:40.382 --> 54:41.383
[polygraph beeping]

710
54:56.273 --> 54:58.275
IS THERE ANY EVENT FROM YOUR CHILDHOOD

711
54:58.358 --> 55:00.319
THAT STANDS OUT IN YOUR MEMORY?

712
55:00.402 --> 55:01.820
When I was nine.

713
55:03.447 --> 55:09.077
A kitten was sitting by the window, looking at me.

714
55:13.665 --> 55:15.208
[examiner] What did you do?

715
55:17.461 --> 55:19.463
I opened the window for it.

716
55:22.716 --> 55:24.635
[examiner] Did the kitten ever come back?

717
55:27.137 --> 55:28.138
No.

718
55:31.933 --> 55:37.981
The kitten ate the chocolate I gave it that day and died.

719
55:49.451 --> 55:51.328
[polygraph beeping]

720
56:18.814 --> 56:20.148
[sniffles]

721
56:20.232 --> 56:23.819
[examiner] Did you feel sexual urges toward Ms. Kang Jisun?

722
56:28.657 --> 56:29.658
Yes.

723
56:31.034 --> 56:35.330
[examiner] Do you remember seeing the kitten dead after eating the chocolate?

724
56:41.795 --> 56:42.796
Yes.

725
56:50.220 --> 56:54.015
Did you sexually assault her that night?

726
57:09.656 --> 57:11.783
[detective retching]

727
57:14.995 --> 57:16.496
-[sighs] -[toilet flushes]

728
57:18.582 --> 57:19.583
[sighs]

729
57:28.675 --> 57:31.845
After breakfast, puke. After lunch, puke.

730
57:31.928 --> 57:35.265
[spouse] I need to have a word with Chubchubs. Let me see.

731
57:38.310 --> 57:40.645
Chubchubs, Daddy's coming home real soon.

732
57:40.729 --> 57:43.648
Until then, don't give my woman a hard time.

733
57:43.732 --> 57:45.859
How about you? How's the food?

734
57:45.942 --> 57:48.236
I'm always eating well.

735
57:48.320 --> 57:49.613
The Navy food's pretty good.

736
57:50.447 --> 57:54.201
But anyway, what if my Hwayoung gets weak from not being able to eat?

737
57:54.284 --> 57:56.995
Well, I blend up anything that's supposed to be good for me

738
57:57.078 --> 57:59.831
and drink it as juice, so I should be getting enough nutrition.

739
57:59.915 --> 58:02.793
NEW EMAIL

740
58:02.876 --> 58:03.877
[spouse] What is it?

741
58:05.420 --> 58:07.589
I got an important email about an investigation.

742
58:08.089 --> 58:13.094
POLYGRAPH TEST RESULTS

743
58:14.846 --> 58:15.847
[clicks mouse]

744
58:19.768 --> 58:20.769
[sighs]

745
58:26.983 --> 58:28.235
[Hwayoung exhales deeply]

746
58:30.362 --> 58:31.655
Where have you been?

747
58:31.738 --> 58:33.031
I was feeling a bit sick.

748
58:35.116 --> 58:36.326
[whispering] Can you tell?

749
58:36.409 --> 58:37.577
Pretty obvious.

750
58:40.038 --> 58:42.374
Secrets don't stay secret for long around here.

751
58:43.667 --> 58:45.585
If I get caught, I'll have to spill.

752
58:45.669 --> 58:49.089
[sighs] I don't know if this will make you feel any better.

753
58:49.172 --> 58:52.175
But my wife was sick for all nine months when she was pregnant.

754
58:52.259 --> 58:53.510
[Hwayoung chuckles]

755
58:53.593 --> 58:55.595
That's a really cruel way to comfort someone.

756
58:56.096 --> 58:57.389
You know me. I don't lie.

757
58:58.056 --> 59:01.518
Oh, right. Did you tell them about the polygraph results?

758
59:04.938 --> 59:06.481
Geez.

759
59:06.565 --> 59:09.192
You can never really know what someone is thinking.

760
59:13.780 --> 59:17.200
I barely eat at home. Why did he make so many side dishes?

761
59:17.284 --> 59:18.660
You know he always goes overboard.

762
59:20.120 --> 59:21.955
Tell Hyeongsu I said thanks.

763
59:22.038 --> 59:23.290
How are you sleeping?

764
59:23.957 --> 59:25.292
Are you getting any sleep?

765
59:27.252 --> 59:28.295
Well, you know…

766
59:30.630 --> 59:33.842
If you don't want to be alone, come stay with us anytime.

767
59:33.925 --> 59:35.302
Hyeongsu said the same.

768
59:36.887 --> 59:39.472
You'll marry Hyeongsu again in your next life, right?

769
59:43.226 --> 59:45.604
[doorbell rings]

770
59:50.567 --> 59:52.485
Looks like you're going to have to hire me.

771
01:00:00.076 --> 01:00:01.077
[door closes]

772
01:00:11.129 --> 01:00:14.299
The polygraph results are in.

773
01:00:18.094 --> 01:00:20.013
[attorney] Something similar happened at the school

774
01:00:20.096 --> 01:00:21.473
where she worked before moving here.

775
01:00:21.973 --> 01:00:25.435
She accused some guy of sexual harassment and completely ruined his life.

776
01:00:25.518 --> 01:00:29.105
PURPOSE OF COMPLAINT THE COMPLAINANT HEREBY FILES…

777
01:00:29.189 --> 01:00:31.191
-[♪ tense music plays] -[objects clattering]

778
01:00:34.110 --> 01:00:36.279
Hey, do you only have rabbit food in your fridge?

779
01:00:41.743 --> 01:00:45.372
[Hwayoung] The analysis found that all of Mr. Min Junho's statements

780
01:00:46.164 --> 01:00:48.541
were truthful.

781
01:00:51.127 --> 01:00:53.964
-[♪ unsettling music plays] -[attorney] She's relentless.

782
01:00:54.047 --> 01:00:56.758
She kept at it until the bitter end and eventually walked away

783
01:00:56.841 --> 01:00:58.301
with a settlement.

784
01:01:00.053 --> 01:01:01.513
You got played by that woman.

785
01:01:08.103 --> 01:01:10.647
You need to fight back and not drag your feet.

786
01:01:10.730 --> 01:01:12.357
Or she'll ruin your life too.

787
01:01:15.235 --> 01:01:17.821
-That can't be true. -You think the truth matters?

788
01:01:17.904 --> 01:01:19.114
What matters is the rumor.

789
01:01:20.156 --> 01:01:21.324
Look around you.

790
01:01:21.408 --> 01:01:23.827
No one cares about the truth. Reputation comes first.

791
01:01:24.911 --> 01:01:26.955
-She's not that kind of woman. -Yes, she is.

792
01:01:27.998 --> 01:01:30.834
She's a repeat offender who plays the victim for money.

793
01:01:34.379 --> 01:01:35.672
What does that mean?

794
01:01:35.755 --> 01:01:37.257
Exactly what I said.

795
01:01:38.842 --> 01:01:41.011
Mr. Min Junho wasn't lying.

796
01:01:44.764 --> 01:01:45.807
How is that possible?

797
01:01:45.890 --> 01:01:48.518
People can remember and interpret the same event differently

798
01:01:49.019 --> 01:01:51.354
depending on their perspective.

799
01:01:56.901 --> 01:01:58.945
I'll tell you your results too.

800
01:01:59.029 --> 01:02:01.698
-Well, of course-- -[Hwayoung] Ms. Kang, your statements…

801
01:02:03.867 --> 01:02:06.161
showed signs of deception.

802
01:02:06.911 --> 01:02:07.912
[♪ music stops]

803
01:02:13.209 --> 01:02:14.461
[♪ dramatic music plays]

804
01:02:14.544 --> 01:02:15.754
That's impossible.

805
01:02:17.630 --> 01:02:20.592
How could the results be so completely wrong?

806
01:02:22.969 --> 01:02:25.305
Something's obviously wrong. It's the exact opposite!

807
01:02:25.388 --> 01:02:28.892
Of the two of you, the one who lied…

808
01:02:33.646 --> 01:02:34.731
is you.

809
01:02:44.699 --> 01:02:48.620
THE PERFECT LIE

810
01:03:12.727 --> 01:03:14.521
[Junho] There must've been a reason.

811
01:03:15.772 --> 01:03:17.732
[Jisun] You want me to admit I lied? Now?

812
01:03:18.608 --> 01:03:20.902
[Junho] Maybe there's something wrong with her psychologically.

813
01:03:20.985 --> 01:03:23.113
-[Hyunsoo] That woman was you? -[doorbell rings]

814
01:03:24.364 --> 01:03:25.990
[attorney] She isn't going to let this go easily.

815
01:03:26.074 --> 01:03:29.160
[Jisun] How am I supposed to have a life after he ruined me like this?

816
01:03:29.244 --> 01:03:32.539
[Junho] What you did impulsively… You're trying to dump all the blame on me.

817
01:03:32.622 --> 01:03:35.166
[Jisun] I'm going to ask them to reinvestigate everything.

818
01:03:35.250 --> 01:03:38.419
[attorney] They say an anonymous woman tipped them off. It's obvious who it was.

819
01:03:38.503 --> 01:03:40.380
[Junho] You got caught lying to me.

820
01:03:41.256 --> 01:03:43.007
And now you're asking me to lie too?

821
01:03:48.930 --> 01:03:50.431
[♪ unsettling music plays]

822
01:03:59.149 --> 01:04:00.775
THE PERFECT LIE

823
01:04:00.859 --> 01:04:02.861
Translated by Liya Hyunjoo Choi3
